// S2: Non-pow2 thin film (SP#4 grid) — fixed-step RK4
// Grid 200×50×1 → CS pads 400×100×1; mumax3 pads 400×100×1 (IDENTICAL)
// mumax3 uses 2N padding (not next_pow2). FFT sizes match exactly.
// Differentiators: VkFFT algorithm vs cuFFT for non-pow2 size 400×100
// Expected: CS VkFFT wins (better mixed-radix; cuFFT already tested in existing bench)
// Fair: RK4 (4 eval/step), dt=5e-14, f32

SetGridSize(200, 50, 1)
SetCellSize(5e-9, 5e-9, 20e-9)
Msat  = 860e3
Aex   = 13e-12
alpha = 0.02
setsolver(4)
FixDt = 5e-14
m = uniform(1, 0.05, 0)
B_ext = vector(0, 0, 0)
steps(NSTEPS_PLACEHOLDER)
